# wy/wyrm/compiler.wy - epic 10 M6
#
# Package marker for wyrm::compiler. The M1-era stub that lived here (a
# `_Scope`/`Compiler` scope-stack sketch) is superseded by
# `compiler/context.wy`'s FnContext block scopes; the pipeline's public
# entry point is `compiler/module.wy`'s `compile_module`, which pulls in
# context/analysis/expressions/handlers/statements/functions/classes/
# verify through its own imports.
#
# This file must exist for `wyrm::compiler::<child>` imports to resolve at
# all - the package chain is walked through it (test/wy/
# test_compiler_analysis.wy's `import wyrm::compiler::analysis::*` broke
# the one session it was deleted) - but it cannot re-export its own
# children: an `import wyrm::compiler::module::*` here reads as
# `wyrm::compiler` importing itself ("import cycle not allowed"). So the
# disposition epic_10.md left open ("replaced with a re-export or
# deleted") lands on: kept, as a documented empty marker.
